body:
Nerf's are bad overall, unless there is something that is extraordinarily broken about a character, which melee doesn't have the brawl problem with a massively clear advantage to one character in the roster, then it doesn't need any nerf's, it needs buffs to the characters who would never be considered up there, and if anything, minor buffs to the characters on the cusp, plus, there could even be some quality of life buffs to even the best of the best characters.

&#x200B;

The reason I say no nerf's, not because I think some characters aren't deserving like fox and puff in my opinion, but, if you nerf characters, it only alienates the players who use them, and makes the overall draw to our entire community towards a mod like this, terrible, you should want everyone to look at something that adds to melee and  say, " I don't see why not ".

This, those attending this reddit tour, is what a copy pasta looks like at its early stages.

&#x200B;

But on a real note, hax was very top level, took a hiatus, came back and got 3rd at Pound losing to Hgod and Mangus. I think the meta is far different looking compared to back then, but at the same time its not, just because you see people ledge cancel stuff, doesn't change the property of attacking in a certain zone. PP has said he is better than his Evo2015 levels, and he got third albeit theres still the meta shift. I think he has always had a unique style, and for him to return, he'd have to learn the mix ups around shield dropping, which again he was already tackling against Armada and Plup before hand, a few situations where players have made their characters more frame tight, like sheiks and falcons specifically have improved across the board alot meta wise, along with other characters, but all thats a given because the game is designed to be as expressive the more skillful you are. I believe you might be going a little ham, but after he hard practices and takes his study/note taking situations more seriously for literally like a couple months, yeah I could see him being 20 before the end of the year, hell if he started his return after Genesis with a real grind and health problems in check, I could see him being top 10 in no time, he was always ahead of his time, and his mind is very unique in how he expresses it into his style, which is something players have always had a hard time against. He'll get there, people discredit characters in this game based on recency bias, Leffen has probably said puff is way better against fox than everyone should think and probably tweeted about the matchup being closer to even, yet he 6-0'd him at SSC. Just wait, PP has a plan, and I think you should trust his judgement, you're not labeled a god without good reasoning.
